\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Across the sky the shades of night
\par This winter's eye are fleeting;
\par We come to Thee, the Life and Light,
\par In solemn worship meeting;
\par And as the year's last hours go by
\par We lift to Thee our earnest cry,
\par Once more Thy love entreating.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Before the Cross subdued we bow,
\par To Thee our prayers addressing;
\par Recounting all Thy mercies now,
\par And all our sins confessing;
\par Beseeching Thee, this coming year,
\par To hold us in Thy faith and fear,
\par And crown us with Thy blessing.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. We gather up in this brief hour,
\par The momory of Thy mercies;
\par Thy wondrous goodness, love, and power
\par Our grateful song rehearses:
\par For Thou hast been our strength and stay
\par In many a dark and dreary day
\par Of sorrow and reverses.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Then, O great God, in years to come,
\par Whatever fate betide us,
\par Right onward through our journey home
\par Be Thou at hand to guide us;
\par Nor leave us till, at close of life,
\par Safe from all peril, toil, and strife,
\par Heaven shall receive and hide us.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

